  "status_text": "One shorter record can answer a whole stack of budget questions. For a process that only moves forward through ordered states, Lean checked that one selection of readings preserves every prefix loss test below its allowed limit, even when different caps on the state have different loss limits (L-meta-53174). The limits can only fall as the state caps rise. The number of readings kept is bounded by the sum of the limits, so the search can reuse one set of readings for all those tests.",
